{% extends "sentence/_base.j2" %}
{#- "*" binds to whatever is being followed, so it is worded that way. A named
    class binds only to the FOLLOWED subject while it carries that class
    (models.SubjectStandoff.binds), never to bystanders of the class, so it is
    worded "the <class> you are following". Until 2026-10-21 it read "any
    <class>", which told the pilot to keep 10 m from every pedestrian when the
    rule binds only the one being followed (open item C8). -#}
{% block core %}Keep at least {{ r.min_range_m|g }} m away from {% if r.subject_class == "*" %}anything you are following{% else %}the {{ r.subject_class }} you are following{% endif %}{% endblock %}
